Article 28. Amendment to provincial housing development programs and plans

1. Amendment to provincial housing development programs shall be conducted upon changes to any of the details specified under Points c, d, dd, or h Clause 1 Article 27 hereof as a result of revision to provincial planning or approval of provincial planning in new stages or establishment, dissolution, merger, acquisition, division, or adjustment to boundaries of provincial administrative divisions.
2. Amended provincial housing development programs shall contain:

a) Necessity for program amendment;
b) Amendment details; funding sources for implementation;

c) Solutions for executing the amendments;

d) Responsibilities of People’s Committees of all levels and local authorities in implementation of amended programs.
3. Amendment to provincial housing development plans of provinces shall be implemented when:

a) Amendment is made to approved provincial housing development programs;
d) Amendment is made to details relating to houses in provincial socio-economic development plans;

c) The case of Clause 4 Article 65 hereof occurs if apartment building renovation, reconstruction plans are developed and approved together with provincial housing development plans.

4. Amended provincial housing development plans shall indicate:
a) Purpose and requirements of revision;

b) Amendment details; funding sources for implementation;
c) Solutions for executing the amendments;

