Article 27. Implementation responsibilities

1. Ministries, central authorities, and the provincial level People’s Committees shall:
a) Report the progress and results of disposition of real estate under their management at the request of competent authorities and persons. The reporting is one of the bases for annually evaluating the performance of the management and use of public property by ministries, central authorities, and local authorities;

b) Organize inspections of compliance with standards and usage of public property within the scope of assigned tasks and authority; organize inspections, checks, urging, and guidance on the disposition of public property in accordance with the provisions of this Decree; handle within their jurisdiction or report to authorities or persons competent to address violations against regulations on management and use of public property as prescribed by law;

c) Direct the agencies, organizations, and units under their management to execute the approved plans of disposition of public property; take full responsibility for organizing the execution of the approved plans;

