4. The unit or organization in charge of compensation, support and resettlement provision shall:

a) cooperate with the People’s Committee of the commune-level administrative division in disseminating and publicly posting the decision to approve the compensation, support and resettlement arrangement at the office of the People’s Committee of the commune-level administrative division and common living area of the residential area to which the repossessed land belongs;

b) send the compensation, support and resettlement arrangement that has been approved by the competent authority to each holder of repossessed land, owner of property affixed to the repossessed land, relevant holder of rights and obligations, which specifies the amount of compensation or support, arrange resettlement house or land (if any), time and place of payment of compensation or support; time for arranging resettlement house or

land (if any) and time for handing over the repossessed land to the unit or organizations in charge of compensation, support and resettlement provision;
c) provide compensation, support or implement resettlement according to the compensation, support and resettlement arrangement which has been approved by the competent authority.

5. The People’s Committee having authority to repossess land shall issue a decision to repossess land within 10 days from the day on which:

a) the compensation, support and resettlement arrangement was approved in case where the resettlement is not required;

