Article 22. Conditions for Recognition and Enforcement of the Court Judgment and Decision

The court judgments and decisions referred to in Article 21 shall be recognized and enforced when all of the following conditions are met:

1. The case does not fall under the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of the Requested Party as prescribed by its national law;

2. The litigants or their legal representatives have been duly summoned or declared absent in accordance with the national law of the Requesting Party;
3. The court judgment or decision has entered into legal effect, and the statute of limitations for enforcement has not expired under the law of the Requesting Party;

4. No final judgment on the same case has been rendered by the courts of the Requested Party or a third country recognized by the Requested Party, and the courts of the Requested Party have not initiated proceedings on the same case at the time of recognition;
5. Recognition and enforcement of the judgment and its consequences do not contravene the fundamental principles of law and public order of the Requested Party.

Article 23. Request for Recognition and Enforcement of Court Judgments

1. A request for recognition and enforcement of a court judgment shall be submitted by the concerned individual or their legal representative to the Central Authority of their own country for transmission to the Central Authority of the Requested Party, or directly to the Central Authority of the Requested Party, in accordance with its laws.

