Article 24. Procedure for Recognition and Enforcement of Court Judgments and Decisions

1. The procedure for recognition and enforcement of court judgments and decisions shall be carried out in accordance with the laws of the Requested Party.
2. The competent authority of the Requested Party shall not review the substance of the judgment or decision to be recognized and enforced.

3. In cases where the competent authority of the Requesting Party sends a written request through its Central Authority to postpone or suspend the recognition and enforcement of the court judgment or decision, the competent authority of the Requested Party shall postpone or suspend the recognition and enforcement accordingly.

Article 25. Effect of Recognition and Enforcement of Court Judgments and Decisions

A court judgment or decision of one Party that has been recognized and enforced by the court of the other Party shall have the same legal effect as a judgment or decision of the court of the latter Party.

