Article 5. Rights and obligations of Vietnamese citizens

1. Vietnamese citizens have the right to:

a) obtain travel documents in accordance with this Law;
b) choose whether to apply for passport with or without electronic chips (for citizens of 14 years of age or older);

c) make entry and exit in accordance with this Law;
d) receive confidentiality for personal secrets, family secrets in the national database of entry and exit of Vietnamese citizens unless information and data disclosure is required as per the law;

dd) request information pertaining to their entry and exit; request updates and revision to information on the national database of entry and exit of Vietnamese citizens and travel documents to ensure that such information is full and accurate;
e) use their passport to conduct transactions or other procedures as per the law;

g) file complaints, denunciations, lawsuits, compensation claims as per the law.

2. Vietnamese citizens have the obligation to:

a) comply with Vietnamese regulations pertaining to entry, exit of Vietnamese citizens and regulations of country of destination when travelling abroad;

b) follow procedures for applying for travel documents, renewal of passports, re-validation of passport in accordance with this Law;
c) use immigration documents issued by Vietnamese competent authorities to make entry and exit;

d) comply with request of competent authorities, competent persons during inspection of person, luggage, travel documents during immigration procedures;

