Article 13. Issuance and renewal of diplomatic passport, official passport in foreign countries

1. Diplomatic passport or official passport in a foreign country shall be issued or renewed in the following cases:

a) Diplomatic passport, official passport is lost, damaged, running out of pages, or expired while the passport holder is on business trip in foreign country;

b) The position of a person who is a member of a Vietnamese representative mission in the foreign country or a governmental press agency or newspaper agency of Vietnam and permanently resides in the foreign country is changed;
c) The person currently residing in the foreign country is assigned to be a member of a Vietnamese representative mission in the foreign country or a governmental press agency or newspaper agency of Vietnam, permanently residing in the foreign country;

d) Spouse or children under 18 years of age, currently residing in the foreign country accompanies or visits the member of a Vietnamese representative mission in the foreign country or a governmental press agency or newspaper agency of Vietnam, permanently residing in the foreign country or the member has a newborn in the foreign country.
2. Applicant for passport issuance or renewal shall submit a completed application, 2 headshots, and relevant documents under clause 3 of this Article to Vietnamese representative mission in the foreign country.

