a) Vietnamese representative missions in foreign countries shall receive requests from competent authorities of host countries or passport applications from individuals rejected to reside by foreign countries, 2 headshots, completed declarations, and identification documents issued by Vietnamese competent authorities (if any);

b) For humanitarian or emergency purposes, where Vietnamese representative missions in foreign countries have sufficient bases to determine identity and nationality of passport applicants, Vietnamese representative missions in foreign countries may consider issuing passports within 2 working days;

c) In respect of cases not specified in point b clause 2 of this Article, within 2 working days from the date on which Vietnamese representative missions in foreign countries receive requests from competent authorities of host countries or applications from individuals rejected to reside by foreign authorities, Vietnamese representative missions in foreign countries shall send information on passport applicants to Immigration Department of the Ministry of Public Security. Within 30 days from the date on which Immigration Department of the Ministry of Public Security receives requests, Immigration Department of the Ministry of Public Security shall conduct verification and send written responses to Vietnamese representative missions in foreign countries.
Within 2 working days from the date on which Vietnamese representative missions in foreign countries receive responses from the Immigration Department of the Ministry of Public Security, Vietnamese representative missions in foreign countries shall issue passports; or issue written responses to the applicants and state reasons in case applications are rejected;

