9. The Minister of National Defense and the Minister of Public Security have the jurisdiction to impose exit suspension for cases under clause 9 Article 36 hereof.
10. Competent persons under clauses 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7 of this Article have the jurisdiction to impose exit suspension only within their tasks and powers and for situations related to the lawsuits and cases within their jurisdiction.

11. Individuals having the jurisdiction to impose exit suspension have the jurisdiction to issue decisions on extension, cancellation of decisions on exit suspension and be legally responsible for their decisions.

12. In special cases, the Minister of Public Security shall discuss with individuals making decisions on exit suspension in order to allow persons suspended from exit to exit Vietnam.

Article 38. Duration of exit suspension, extension of exit suspension

1. Duration of exit suspension, extension of exit suspension:
a) For cases under clause 1 Article 36 hereof, duration of exit suspension shall conform to the Criminal Proceeding Code;

b) For cases under clauses 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6 Article 36 hereof, duration of exit suspension shall only end where offenders or people with obligations fulfill judgments or decisions of competent agencies, competent persons according to this Law;

c) For cases under clause 7 Article 36 hereof, duration of exit suspension shall not be longer than 1 year and can be extended for at most 1 year each time;

d) For cases under clause 8 Article 36 hereof, duration of exit suspension shall not be longer than 6 months and can be extended for at most 6 months each time;

