The rights and obligations of the denouncers and denounced parties in the implementation of educational measures at reform schools shall be carried out in accordance with the Law on denunciation.

Article 20. Authority to resolve denunciations and supervise the resolution of denunciations

1. The authority of the People's Public Security Forces to resolve denunciations is as follows:

a) The Principal of the reform school and the Head of the Criminal judgment execution agency of the Provincial Police authority shall resolve denunciations regarding violations against the law by individuals under their management;

b) The Head of the Criminal judgment execution management agency of the Ministry of Public Security shall resolve denunciations regarding violations against the law by the Principal of the reform school and violations of the law by individuals under their management; the Director of the Provincial police authority shall resolve denunciations regarding violations against the law by the Head of the Criminal judgment execution management agency of the Provincial police authority;

c) The Minister of Public Security shall resolve denunciations regarding violations of the law by the Head of the Criminal judgment execution management agency of the Ministry of Public Security.

2. The authority of the Courts to resolve denunciations is as follows:

a) The Chief Justice of the Regional People's Court and the Chief Justice of the Regional Military Court shall resolve denunciations regarding violations of Judges, Court Investigators, Court Clerks, and Deputy Chief Justices of the Regional People's Court and Regional Military Court under their management;

b) The Chief Justice of the Provincial People's Court shall resolve denunciations regarding violations of Chief Justice of the Regional People's Court; the Chief Justice of the Military Court of the military zone shall resolve denunciations regarding violations of the Chief Justice of the Regional Military Court;

