Chapter III

INITIATION, ACCEPTANCE AND SETTLEMENT OF CIVIL PUBLIC INTEREST LAWSUITS

Article 14. Initiation of civil public interest lawsuits

1. Within 02 months from the date of expiry of the time limit specified in clause 3, Article 13 of this Resolution, if there is no plaintiff or the Procuracy does not receive a written response from any agency, organization or individual that has the right and responsibility to initiate lawsuit, the Procuracy shall consider deciding to:

a) Initiate a lawsuit to protect public interests;

b) Initiate a lawsuit to protect civil rights of persons in the vulnerable group when the person whose civil rights are infringed or his/her legal representative is unable to initiate a lawsuit and requests the Procuracy to initiate a lawsuit; in case where there is a ground to determine that such person fails to initiate a lawsuit due to deception, threat, coercion or mistake, the Procuracy shall consider deciding to initiate the lawsuit.

2. Decision to initiate a civil public interest lawsuit shall contain the main contents, including:
a) Name of the Procuracy that initiates the lawsuit;

b) Name and address of the defendant;
c) Name and address of the protected agency/organization/individual;

d) Name and address of the person having relevant interests and obligations, and the witness;

dd) Rights and interests infringed;
e) Request for initiation of the lawsuit and reasons.

3 . Within 05 working days from the date of issuance, the Procuracy shall send such decision enclosed with documents and evidence to the Court that has the jurisdiction to settle the lawsuit.

4. When initiating a lawsuit, the Procuracy is not required to pay a court fee advance or pay court fee. The Procuracy that requests the application of provisional emergency measures is not required to implement security measures; in case the application of provisional emergency measures is incorrect and causes damage, compensation must be paid according to the Law on State Compensation Liability.

