Article 38. Jurisdiction of specialized tribunals of People’s Courts of provinces

1. Civil tribunals of People’s Courts of provinces shall have the jurisdiction to:
a) Resolve, according to first-instance procedures, civil disputes/petitions within the jurisdiction of People’s Courts of provinces specified in Article 37 of this Code;

b) Resolve, according to appellate procedures, cases where the civil judgments/decisions of People’s Courts of districts that are not legally effective and are appealed against according to regulations in this Code.

2. Family and juvenile tribunals of People’s Courts of provinces shall have the jurisdiction to:

a) Resolve, according to first-instance procedures, disputes/petitions related to marriage and family falling within the jurisdiction of People’s Courts of provinces specified in Article 37 of this Code;

b) Resolve, according to appellate procedures, cases where the judgments/decisions related to marriage and family of People’s Courts of districts that are not legally effective and are appealed against according to regulations in this Code.
3. Economic tribunals of People’s Courts of provinces shall have the jurisdiction to:

a) Resolve, according to first-instance procedures, disputes/petitions related to business and trade within the jurisdiction of People’s Courts of provinces specified in Article 37 of this Code;

b) Resolve, according to appellate procedures, cases where the judgments/decisions related to business and trade of People’s Courts of districts that are not legally effective and are appealed against according to regulations in this Code.

4. Labor tribunals of People’s Courts of provinces shall have the jurisdiction to:
a) Resolve, according to first-instance procedures, labor disputes/petitions within the jurisdiction of People’s Courts of provinces specified in Article 37 of this Code;

b) Resolve, according to appellate procedures, cases where labor judgments/decisions of People’s Courts of districts that are not legally effective and are appealed against according to regulations in this Code.

