2. When the Chief Justice is absent, a Deputy-Chief Justice shall be authorized by the Chief Justice to perform the Chief Justice's tasks and powers, excluding the right to file appeals prescribed in point g clause 1 of this Article. The Deputy-Chief Justice shall be responsible to the Chief Justice for the authorized tasks and powers.

Article 48. Tasks and powers of Judges

As assigned by the Court’s Chief Justice, the Judge shall have the following tasks and powers:

1. Proceed the application for initiating lawsuits and the petitions and accept the civil cases according to regulations in this Code;
2. File dossiers on civil cases;

3. Collect and verify evidence, hold Court sessions and meetings to resolve civil cases according to regulations in this Code;
4. Decide to apply, change or cancel provisional emergency measures;

5. Decide to suspend or terminate the resolution of civil cases and decide to continue the resolution of the civil cases;

6. Provide explanation and guidance for the involved parties so that they can exercise the right to apply for legal assistance according to law on legal assistance;

7. Hold meetings for inspection of the handover of, access to and disclosure of evidences and mediation and issue decisions on recognition of the agreements among the involved parties according to regulations of this Code;
8. Decide to bring civil lawsuits to Court for trial, or bring civil matters for resolution;

9. Convene people to a trial or a meeting;
10. Act as the chairperson or participate in adjudication of civil lawsuits and resolution of civil matters;

11. Request the Court’s Chief Justice to assign ombudspersons to assist in following civil proceedings according to regulations of this Code;

