Article 58. Tasks and powers of procurators

When assigned by the Chief Procurator to supervise the law observance in civil proceedings, a procurator shall have the following tasks and powers:
1. Supervise the return of the petition;

2. Supervise acceptance and resolution of civil cases;

3. Study case files; request the Court to verify and collect evidences during the resolution of civil cases according to regulations of this Code; collect materials and evidences according to regulations in clause 6 Article 97 of this Code;

4. Attend Court sessions/meetings and express opinions of the procuracy about the resolution of cases according to regulations of this Code;

5. Inspect judgments/decisions of the Court;

6. Request the Court to conduct procedural activities as provided for in this Code;
7. Request a competent Chief Procurator to appeal against judgments/decisions of the Court that are contrary to law;

