Article 70. Rights and obligations of the involved parties

The involved parties shall have equal rights and obligations when participating in civil procedures. When participating in civil procedures, the involved parties shall have the following rights and obligations:

1. Respect Courts, and strictly observe Courts’ rules;
2. Advance Court fees and charges and pay Court fees and charges and other expenses as prescribed by law;

3. Sufficiently and accurately provide addresses of their residence/work places; during the resolution of cases, any change of addresses of residence/workplaces shall be promptly notified to other involved parties and Courts;

4. Maintain, modify, supplement or withdraw their petitions in accordance with this Code;

5. Supply materials and evidences; offer proof to protect their legitimate rights and interests;

6. Petition agencies, organizations and individuals that are keeping or managing materials and evidences to supply such materials and evidences to them;

7. Petition Courts to verify and collect materials and evidences of the cases which they cannot perform themselves; petition Courts to request other involved parties to present materials and evidences they are keeping; petition Courts to issue decisions to request agencies, organizations and individuals that are keeping and managing materials/evidences to supply such materials and evidences; request Courts to summon witnesses, to ask for expertise, evaluation or price appraisal;

8. Read and take notes, make photocopies of materials and evidences produced by other involved parties or collected by Courts, except for materials and evidences specified in clause 2 Article 109 of this Code;

9. Send other involved parties or their lawful representatives photocopies of petitions and materials and evidences, excluding evidences and materials owned by other involved parties or with evidences and materials as prescribed in clause 2 Article 109 of this Code.

