Unless otherwise agreed by involved parties or provided for by laws, the obligation to incur the overseas judicial entrustment expense shall be determined as follows:

1. The involved parties shall incur the overseas judicial entrustment expense if their requests for settlement of cases are rejected by the Court;

2. In case where the Court is requested to divide a common property, each person who has received a share from such property shall bear incur the overseas judicial entrustment expense proportionate to the value of the property share he/she has received;
3. In divorce cases, plaintiffs shall pay overseas judicial entrustment expenses, regardless of whether the Courts accept their requests or not. In cases where both parties voluntarily agree on their divorce, each involved party must bear half of the overseas judicial entrustment expense;

4. If the lawsuit settlement is suspended as prescribed in point c clause 1 Article 217, point b clause 1 Article 299 of this Code, the plaintiff shall incur the overseas judicial entrustment expense.

If the matter settlement according to appellate procedures is suspended as prescribed in point b clause 1 Article 289, clause 3 Article 296 of this Code, the appellant according to appellate procedures shall incur the overseas judicial entrustment expense;
5. For other cases where the lawsuit settlement is suspended according to regulations of this Code, the person who petitions for overseas judicial entrustment shall incur the overseas judicial entrustment expense.

Article 154. Handling of advanced expenses on overseas judicial entrustment

1. If the person who has paid the advanced expense on overseas judicial entrustment is not liable for the overseas judicial entrustment expense, the person who has to bear such expense under the decision issued by the Court shall refund the advanced expense to the former.

