6. Relevant agencies, organizations and individuals.

Article 3. Definitions

1. Digital platforms used for the notification of procedural documents under this Joint Circular include:

a) Web portals and websites of authorities conducting criminal proceedings;
b) The National Public Service Portal and information systems for administrative procedure settlement of regulatory agencies and ministries and sectors;

c) The National Electronic Identity Application (VNeID);

d) Other digital platforms that fully satisfy the requirements on protection of state secrets, cybersecurity, information security and personal data protection.

2. Specialized software means electronic software designed, developed, managed and independently used by ministries and sectors, integrated in the case file database to serve digital signing and digitization of case files activities, and used continuously throughout the stages of institution of criminal proceedings, investigation, prosecution and adjudication, and the execution of criminal judgments. Specialized software enables data connectivity, sharing and interoperability among commune-level police authorities, police posts, competent authorities conducting criminal proceedings, and agencies managing and enforcing pre-trial detention and executing criminal judgments.
3. Case file database means a system compiling information, documents and data structured according to data architecture, data standards and common data standards, for the management, retrieval, interoperability-based connection and data extraction among national databases, sector-specific databases, information systems and the National Data Center. The case file database shall be initialized, converted and integrated in specialized software by authorized persons in accordance with Article 18 of this Joint Circular.

