Article 23. Implementation

1. The Ministry of Public Security, Ministry of National Defense, Supreme People's Procuracy and Supreme People's Court shall, within the scope of their respective duties and powers, be responsible for:
a) Developing, upgrading, completing and managing specialized software, the case file database, technical infrastructure and other conditions for digital signing of procedural documents and digitization of case files, ensuring data security and confidentiality; reaching agreement on the content of information, documents and data authorized for sharing;

b) Developing and issuing common data catalogs/standards (case/incident identifier codes; document codes, folio marks; physical evidence codes; procedural party codes and related standard lists); procedures for connecting, testing and ensuring interoperability among systems to maintain stable and continuous operation of the connection system; monitoring, inspecting and logging connection activities, detecting, preventing and handling information security and cybersecurity incidents during data exchange and interoperability;
c) Issuing procedures and guidelines for agencies under their management on digital signing, digitization of case files, creation of new data, supplementary digitization of procedural documents and data; procedures for implementing alternative authentication methods other than electronic signatures of participants in criminal proceedings;

d) Issuing procedures and guidelines for the delivery, transfer, receipt, transmission, notification and execution of electronic procedural documents and e-case files; guiding the notification procedures for procedural documents via digital platforms and shared application software deployed in the National Data Center, in accordance with the functions of each ministry and sector;
dd) Coordinating inter-agency efforts to supplement operational functions and technical, security and information security requirements of specialized software; monitoring data connectivity and synchronization, handling technical failures and ensuring data integrity during operation.

