Article 41. Duties, authority and responsibilities of Chief Prosecutors and Deputy Chief Prosecutors of

Procuracies
1. The Chief Prosecutor of a Procuracy shall bear the following duties and authority:

a) Directly organize and command the activities of exercising prosecution rights and supervising legal compliance of criminal procedure;

b) Decide to appoint or replace Deputy Chief Prosecutors of the Procuracy, inspect deputy heads’ activities of exercising prosecution rights and supervising legal compliance of criminal procedure, decide to redress or annul groundless and lawless decisions made by deputy heads;

c) Decide to appoint or replace procurators and checkers, inspect and manage procurators’ and checkers’ activities of exercising prosecution rights and supervising legal compliance in criminal proceedings, decide to redress or vacate unfounded and illegal decisions made by procurators;

d) Decide to remove, terminate or annul unproven and illicit decisions made by an inferior Procuracy;

dd) Handle complaints and accusations within the powers of the Procuracy.

The Chief Prosecutor of the Procuracy, upon his absence, mandates a deputy head to perform his duties and authority and assume liabilities before the head for the duties mandated.

2. When exercising prosecution rights and supervising legal compliance in criminal proceedings, the Chief Prosecutor of the Procuracy bears the following duties and authority:

a) Request investigation authorities and authorities tasked with conducting certain investigational activities to process criminal information, press charges or amend decisions on filing criminal lawsuits or charges against suspects; decide to press or not to file charges, redress decisions on filing criminal lawsuits or charges against defendants as per this Code;

