Article 153. Authority to press criminal charges

1. Investigation authorities shall make decisions on pressing criminal charges against all matters exhibiting criminal signs, save those handled by authorities tasked with conducting certain investigational activities, procuracies or juries as per clause 2, 3 and 4 in this Article.

2. Authorities tasked with conducting certain investigational activities shall make decisions on pressing criminal charges in the events as defined in Article 164 of this Code.

3. The Procuracy makes decisions on pressing criminal charges in the following events:

a) The Procuracy decides to rescind a decision not to press criminal charges from investigation authorities or authorities tasked with conducting certain investigational activities;
b) The Procuracy directly processes denunciations, information and requisitions;

