1. Comply with this Decree and relevant laws; and ensure the participation and cooperation of agencies, organizations, individuals, and families in implementing measures to ensure community reintegration.
2. Create favorable conditions for persons having completely served prison sentences to reintegrate into the community and stabilize their lives, and prevent recidivism and violations of the law.

3. It is strictly prohibited to stigmatize or discriminate against inmates and persons having completely served prison sentences or infringe upon their lawful rights and interests.

Article 4. Funding for community reintegration

1. State funding for community reintegration shall be allocated in the annual recurrent expenditure estimates of agencies and units in accordance with the current decentralization of the state budget. Subject to budget decentralization, budget-balancing capacity, and the expenditure standards and norms prescribed by law, the state budget shall cover the following:

a) Expenditures on professional training and refresher training for persons engaged in community reintegration;

b) Expenditures on support for persons who directly assist persons having completely served prison sentences;
c) Expenditures on publicizing and disseminating the contents of this Decree; expenditures on organizing conferences and training courses and on legal dissemination and education to raise awareness among the community, inmates, and persons having completely served prison sentences who reside in local areas;

d) Expenditures on vocational training support as prescribed in Clause 1 Article 9 of this Decree;
dd) Expenditures on organizing preliminary and final reviews, commendation, and rewards; and developing, maintaining, and replicating community reintegration models;

e) Expenditures on developing, maintaining, and upgrading data management software systems serving community reintegration;

