CÁC NỘI DUNG CHUẨN BỊ TÁI HÒA NHẬP CỘNG ĐỒNG CHO PHẠM NHÂN

Điều 5. Tư vấn tâm lý, hỗ trợ các thủ tục pháp lý cho phạm nhân

source:
1. Within 2 months before an inmate completely serves their prison sentence, or after the competent authority issues its appraisal results regarding the proposal to grant amnesty or conditional early release, the inmate detention facility shall organize psychological counseling and provide assistance with legal procedures for the inmate.

2. Psychological counseling is intended to provide inmates with knowledge and guidance and enhance their ability to independently resolve difficulties and problems arising during community reintegration. Counseling shall cover:
a) Emotional relationships, marriage, family and health; and prevention and control of drugs, HIV/AIDS, and social evils;

b) Overcoming feelings of stigma and inferiority; building willpower and confidence; and improving the ability to cope with and resolve issues arising during community reintegration;

c) Labor and employment; use of acquired vocational skills; social insurance; and other relevant matters.

3. Methods of providing psychological counseling for inmates:
a) Inmate detention facilities shall arrange for inmates to register their counseling needs using forms specifying the matters on which they require counseling, or proactively identify inmates’ problems that require counseling, and shall then assign officers with experience and knowledge in relevant fields to provide inmates with direct counseling. Counseling may be provided individually to each inmate or in groups of inmates who require counseling on the same matters;

b) Individual counseling shall be conducted in counseling rooms or other appropriate locations that ensure privacy and safety and are equipped with desks, chairs, and other facilities necessary for counseling.
4. Inmates preparing to completely serve their prison sentences, be granted amnesty, or be granted conditional early release shall receive counseling and guidance on carrying out necessary legal procedures, including residence registration; issuance or replacement of identity cards; borrowing loans; business registration;

