source:
MEASURES TO ENSURE COMMUNITY REINTEGRATION FOR PERSONS HAVING COMPLETELY SERVED PRISON SENTENCES

Article 8. Information, communication, and education regarding community reintegration

1. Information, communication, and education regarding community reintegration are intended to guide and encourage the community to participate in assisting persons having completely served prison sentences;
eliminate prejudice, stigma, and discrimination; and raise awareness and a sense of compliance with the law, thereby contributing to preventing recidivism and violations of the law by persons having completely served prison sentences.

2. Contents of information, communication, and education regarding community reintegration:
a) The guidelines and policies of the CPV and the policies and laws of the State regarding community reintegration;

b) The rights and obligations of citizens and persons having completely served prison sentences as prescribed by law;

c) Measures, experience, models, and exemplary practices in educating and assisting persons having completely served prison sentences and eliminating prejudice, stigma, and discrimination against them;

