Article 10. Psychological assistance and assistance with legal procedures

1. Psychological assistance is intended to strengthen the confidence, willpower, and resilience of persons having completely served prison sentences, support their community reintegration, and prevent violations of the law.
Such assistance includes eliminating feelings of stigma and inferiority; developing life skills and community integration skills; and improving their ability to independently resolve difficulties and problems in social relationships.

Psychological assistance shall be provided as soon as persons having completely served prison sentences return to their places of residence in the following forms:

a) Individual or group counseling;
b) Provision of information and materials according to their needs;

c) Community activities, forums, and thematic sessions;
d) Counseling through cyberspace, websites, email, telephone, and other information and communication media.

