3. Participants in a community reintegration model include:

a) A Model Steering Committee headed by the President of the People’s Committee at the same level, with representatives of the leadership of the Public Security authority at the same level, the Vietnam Fatherland Front Committee at the same level, and relevant agencies and organizations as members;

b) Entities participating in implementing the model, including representatives of relevant departments, divisions, boards, and sectors; socio-political organizations; enterprises, vocational education institutions, employment service providers; and the residential community in the local area where the model is implemented;

c) Persons participating in the model who are persons having completely served prison sentences;

d) Members of the Model Steering Committee and agencies and organizations participating in the model shall work on a part-time basis; the Model Steering Committee shall automatically dissolve upon completion of the model.

4. Procedures for developing a community reintegration model:

a) Provincial-level and commune-level Public Security authorities shall, within their respective management scopes, assume the prime responsibility for advising the People’s Committees at the same level on developing plans to survey and assess local conditions. Each plan shall contain the following principal contents: survey contents, methods, time and scope; data collection methods; and data consolidation;

b) Provincial-level and commune-level Public Security authorities shall, within their respective management scopes, collect and consolidate information on local conditions, population characteristics, and the number of persons having completely served prison sentences who return to the local area, including the number of persons who need loans, vocational training, or employment support, and the conditions for ensuring community reintegration;

