ELABORATING THE LAW ON PREVENTION AND COMBAT OF HUMAN TRAFFICKING
Pursuant to the Law on Government Organization dated February 18, 2025;

Pursuant to the Law on Local Government Organization dated June 16, 2025;
Pursuant to the Law on Prevention and Combat of Human Trafficking dated November 28, 2024;

At request of Minister of Health;
The Government promulgates Decree elaborating the Law on Prevention and Combat of Human Trafficking.

Chapter I

GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1. Scope

1. Elaborate Clause 6 Article 27, Clause 3 Article 28, Clause 5 Article 29, Clause 3 Article 30, Clause 7 Article 31, Clause 6 Article 35, Clause 5 Article 37, Clause 7 Article 46, Clause 4 Article 47, Clause 3 Article 56 of the Law on Prevention and Combat of Human Trafficking.

2. Prescribe solutions and guidelines for implementation of Clause 3 Article 22 of the Law on Prevention and Combat of Human Trafficking.

Article 2. Regulated entities

This Decree applies to agencies, organizations, and individuals engaged in prevention and combat of human trafficking; human trafficking victim support facilities, other social support facilities; human trafficking victims, persons under victim identification process, and accompanying persons under 18 years of age; relatives of human trafficking victims; relatives of persons under victim identification process; agencies, organizations, and individuals related to prevention and combat of human trafficking.

Article 3. Expenditure on implementation

1. Funding sources for human trafficking victim identification, determination, protection, and support:

a) State budget;
b) Funding for criminal prevention and combat;

c) Contributions made by domestic and foreign organizations, individuals;
d) Other legitimate funding sources as per the law.

