d) Within 3 working days from the date on which Chairpersons of provincial People’s Committees receive request for reissuance, amendment, supplement of human trafficking victim support license from Departments of Health, Chairpersons of provincial People’s Committees shall consider and issue decision on issuance, amendment, supplement of human trafficking victim support license using Form No. 20 under Appendix attached hereto. Where the application is rejected, Chairpersons of provincial People’s Committees shall respond in writing and state reasons.

Article 42. Suspension and revocation of human trafficking victim support license

1. Chairpersons of provincial People’s Committees shall issue decision on suspension of human trafficking victim support where human trafficking victim support facilities fail to satisfy any of the requirements under
Article 38 hereof depending on registered service at which point human trafficking facilities are suspended for 6

months in order to fulfill operation requirements.
2. Chairpersons of provincial People's Committees shall issue decision on revocation of human trafficking victim support license where:

a) License is issued in a manner that does not respect entitlement or does not conform to regulations of the law;
b) Human trafficking victim support facilities do not operate for 12 months from the date on which license is issued;

c) Human trafficking victim support facilities change operating purposes in a manner that does not conform to regulations of the law;
d) Human trafficking victim support facilities fail to satisfy requirements by the end of suspension period;

