Article 44. Transition clause

1. Other social support facilities that provide support for human trafficking victims established by competent authorities and entering into operation before the effective date hereof shall be required to inform Departments of Health of administrative divisions where the facilities are located within 30 days from the effective date hereof and file quarterly, 6-monthly, and annual reports on support provided for human trafficking victims, persons under victim determination process, and accompanying persons under 18 years of age.
2. In case of issues that require resolutions following arrangement of organizational structure, agencies that acquire functions, tasks, and powers have the responsibility to cooperate with relevant agencies in resolving issues that arise.

3. Documents processed prior to the effective date hereof and unfinished shall be further processed in accordance with Decree No. 09/2013/ND-CP and Decree No. 62/2012/ND-CP.

Article 45. Responsibility for implementation

1. Ministry of Health shall:
a) arrange implementation of this Decree and provide guidelines on implementation of this Decree within their tasks and powers;

b) take charge of reviewing, studying, developing, amending legislative documents and relevant documents on human trafficking prevention and combat and human trafficking victim support within their tasks and powers;

c) provide guidelines on operation of national hotline for human trafficking prevention and combat; procedures, standards, quality of human trafficking victim support services; survey and early intervention for groups suspected of falling victim to human trafficking; develop regulations on interdisciplinary cooperation in reception, protection, and support for human trafficking victims, persons under victim determination process;

2. Ministry of Public Security shall:
a) arrange implementation of this Decree and provide guidelines on implementation of this Decree within their tasks and powers;

