6. Provincial People’s Committees shall:
a) arrange local implementation within their functions and duties under the Law on Prevention and Combat of Human Trafficking and this Decree;

b) promulgate programs, plans, projects, schemes for human trafficking prevention and control; allocate resources for human trafficking prevention and combat tasks;

c) direct commune-level People’s Committees to prioritize resources for implementation of human trafficking prevention and combat tasks in their jurisdiction;

d) enable other facilities to assist in human trafficking prevention and combat; support service providers for human trafficking victims to operate in their jurisdiction;

dd) promptly commend and award within their powers or request competent authorities to commend, praise excellent groups, individuals in human trafficking prevention and combat;

e) request equivalent People’s Councils to decide specific support solutions and policies for human trafficking prevention and combat and support for human trafficking victims, persons under victim determination process, and accompanying persons under 18 years of age;

g) Chairpersons of provincial People’s Committees shall be responsible for human trafficking prevention and combat in their jurisdiction.

7. Ministers, heads of ministerial agencies, heads of Governmental agencies, Chairpersons of People's Committees of provinces and central-affiliated cities, and relevant agencies, organizations, individuals shall be responsible for the implementation of this Decree./.

ON BEHALF OF THE GOVERNMENT PP. PRIME MINISTER DEPUTY PRIME MINISTER

Le Thanh Long

