Article 9. Regulations applicable to persons coming to meet, visit, or hold consular contact with an inmate,

or to work at or cooperate in organizing educational activities at a detention facility
1. A person coming to meet, visit, or hold consular contact with an inmate, or to work at or cooperate in organizing educational, labor, vocational orientation, vocational training, healthcare, or other activities at a detention facility shall wear the uniform prescribed by the Charter of the People's Public Security Force or the regulations of their agency, unit, or enterprise; in other cases, they must wear neat, clean, and formal attire; and present documents or other means to establish that they are a person with the authority or responsibility to work at, or to cooperate in organizing activities at the detention facility.

