The written notice shall specify the full name; date of birth; nationality; reason for temporary custody or temporary detention; term of temporary custody or temporary detention; place of temporary custody or temporary detention; and contact point of the case-handling agency, and shall be enclosed with a copy of the identity document of the person held in temporary custody or temporary detention.
2. After receiving the written notice from the case-handling agency, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Vietnam shall immediately notify the relevant diplomatic mission or consular post of the temporary custody or temporary detention of the foreigner and request confirmation of the nationality of the person held in temporary custody or temporary detention (where necessary). Within 3 working days from receipt of the result, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Vietnam shall notify the case-handling agency in writing. The case-handling agency shall immediately notify the detention facility of such matters for cooperation in management.

Article 6. Organization of consular contact for foreign persons held in temporary custody or temporary

detention
1. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Vietnam shall act as the focal point for receiving requests for consular contact. A foreign diplomatic mission or consular post requesting consular contact with a person held in temporary custody or temporary detention who is a national of its country shall submit a written request to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Vietnam. The written request shall contain:

a) Name of the diplomatic mission or consular post;
b) Full name and nationality of the person held in temporary custody or temporary detention with whom consular contact is requested;

c) The detention facility managing the person held in temporary custody or temporary detention;
d) Full names, positions, and passport numbers or numbers of diplomatic identity cards, consular identity cards, or honorary consular identity cards of the persons coming to have consular contact with the person held in temporary custody or temporary detention;

dd) Full name and identity-document number of the interpreter (if any);
e) Proposed time of consular contact (if any);

g) Contents of the consular contact and other requests (if any).

