4. The head of the detention facility shall not approve consular contact in the cases prescribed in Points b, c, d, and h Clause 4 Article 22 of the Law on Enforcement of Temporary Custody, Temporary Detention, and Prohibition from Leaving Place of Residence. Once the reason for not approving consular contact no longer exists, the detention facility shall cooperate with the case-handling agency in notifying the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Vietnam, which shall notify the foreign diplomatic mission or consular post of such matters.
5. Where a person held in temporary custody or temporary detention refuses consular contact, the detention facility shall make minutes recording the refusal, bearing the signature or fingerprint of that person and the signature of a witness.

Article 7. Organization of contact with humanitarian organizations for foreign persons held in temporary

custody or temporary detention
1. Where an international treaty to which the Socialist Republic of Vietnam is a contracting party or an agreement between Vietnam and a relevant country designates a focal-point agency for receiving requests from humanitarian organizations, the humanitarian organization shall submit a written request to the focal-point agency designated in that international treaty or international agreement. The written request shall contain:

a) Name of the humanitarian organization and documents relating to its operations;
b) Full name and nationality of the person held in temporary custody or temporary detention for whom contact with the humanitarian organization is requested;

c) The detention facility managing the person held in temporary custody or temporary detention;
d) Full name, position, and identity document of the representative of the humanitarian organization coming to have contact;

dd) Full name and identity document of the interpreter (if any);
e) Proposed time of contact (if any);

g) Contents of the contact and other requests (if any).

