4. Responsibilities of agencies, organizations, and individuals for providing and using information and data on enforcement of temporary custody, temporary detention, and prohibition from leaving place of residence:

a) Upon request, provide information falling within the scope of their functions, duties, and entitlements for the development of the database on enforcement of temporary custody, temporary detention, and prohibition from leaving place of residence, and assume responsibility for the accuracy of the information they provide;
b) Use information for the proper purpose; comply with laws on state secret protection, personal data protection, and information safety and security; and promptly notify the competent data-managing agency of errors in the provided data;

c) Lodge complaints and denunciations in accordance with the law when their rights to access and use data are infringed upon.

