Article 5. Equipment and hiring of professional technical equipment and devices

1. Authority to decide on equipping professional technical equipment and devices

a) Directors General of the Department for Roads of Vietnam, Vietnam Maritime and Inland Waterway Administration, Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam, and Vietnam Railway Authority shall decide on equipping professional technical equipment and devices for their respective departments and affiliated authorities/units in accordance with laws on management and use of public assets, laws on the state budget, and relevant laws.

b) Province-level People's Committees shall decide on equipping professional technical equipment and devices for Departments of Construction and units.

2. The regime and funding for equipping and hiring professional technical equipment and devices shall comply with Articles 7, 8, and 9 of Decree No. 61/2026/ND-CP and relevant laws.

3. Directors General of the Department for Roads of Vietnam, Vietnam Maritime and Inland Waterway Administration, Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam, and Vietnam Railway Authority; Directors of Departments of Construction; heads of units assigned by province-level People's Committees shall prepare plans and cost estimates for the investment, purchase, equipment, maintenance, repair, inspection, calibration, and testing of professional technical equipment and devices, and for purchase of consumable supplies serving the operation of such equipment and devices, and submit them to competent authorities in accordance with laws on the state budget.

Article 6. Management, use, and operation of professional technical equipment and devices

1. Units managing, using, and operating professional technical equipment and devices include:

a) Department for Roads of Vietnam and affiliated units;
b) Vietnam Railway Authority and affiliated units;

c) Vietnam Maritime Inspectorate; Inland Waterways Administrations; Maritime Administrations;
d) Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam Inspectorate; Airport Authorities;

