Article 14. Use and preservation of results collected by professional technical equipment and devices

1. The use and preservation of results collected by professional technical equipment and devices shall comply with Article 64 of the Law on Penalties for Administrative Violations, and the following regulations:

a) Authorities and units using results collected by professional technical equipment and devices to detect administrative violations are responsible for arranging appropriate storage locations, necessary equipment, and implementing technical measures to ensure safe and confidentiality of information and documents in accordance with laws on archive and relevant laws;

b) Results collected by professional technical equipment and devices shall be recorded into dossiers on administrative violation cases.

2. The results collected by professional technical equipment and devices shall be recorded in writing including the following information:

a) Name of the agency or unit, signature and full name of the user of professional technical equipment and devices;
b) Name and address of the violator (if identified);

c) Images (for recording devices, vehicle speed measuring devices with image recording); audio recordings (for audio recording devices);

d) Measurement and analysis indices (for equipment with measuring, analyzing or testing functions);
dd) Time and place of the violation;

e) The violated act or conclusion on measurement, analysis or testing results;
g) Other information related to the violation (if any).

