3. The validity period for using results collected by professional technical equipment and devices to impose administrative penalties on violators shall be determined from the time on which the equipment records the results until the last day of the prescriptive period for imposition of penalties as prescribed in clause 1, Article 6 of the Law on Penalties for Administrative Violations.
If competent authorities do not issue a decision on imposing penalties prescribed time limit, the results collected by professional technical equipment and devices shall no longer be valid as grounds for imposing penalties.

Article 15. Handling of results collected by professional technical equipment and devices

1. When results are collected by professional technical equipment and devices, competent authorities handling administrative violations as prescribed by laws on penalties for administrative violations shall perform the following steps:

a) Identify information about violators;
b) Send a written notification requesting violators to present themselves at the office of competent authorities for resolution, except in cases where competent authorities have already identified violators, and relevant entities (if any) at the location, route or area where violations occurred and have prepared the administrative violation record;

c) Prepare the administrative violation record within 05 working days from the date on which violators is identified by professional technical equipment and devices;

d) Issue decisions on imposing administrative penalties and organize the enforcement of such decisions as prescribed by laws.

