Competent authorities may conduct verification, collect information and clarify the case by one or more of the following methods:

a) Use equipped professional technical equipment and devices to detect and determine administrative violations;
b) Work with individuals or organizations that provided the data; individuals or organizations reported for administrative violations; relevant individuals or organizations; witnesses or persons who know about the case to collect relevant information and documents;

a) Comply with Article 64 of the Law on Penalties for Administrative Violations, and relevant laws in this Decree;

b) Persons using technical equipment and devices are employees of organizations owning equipment and devices in accordance with requirements and responsibilities as prescribed in Article 13 of this Decree;

c) The handling of results collected by technical equipment and devices shall comply with Article 15 of this Decree.

Chapter IV

IMPLEMENTATION PROVISIONS

Article 23. Effect

1. This Decree comes into force from April 01, 2026.
2. The following regulations are annulled:

a) Decree No. 135/2021/ND-CP dated December 31, 2021 of the Government on the list, management and use of professional technical equipment and devices; procedures for collection and use of data collected by technical equipment and devices that are provided by individuals and organizations for detection of administrative violations;
b) Article 60 of Decree No. 38/2024/ND-CP dated April 05, 2024 of the Government on penalties for administrative violations against regulations on fisheries;

c) Article 21 of Decree No. 184/2025/ND-CP dated July 01, 2025 of the Government on decentralization of authority regarding 02-level local government organization; and amendments to some articles of Decrees of the Government in the field of security and order.

Article 24. Transition clauses

1. Professional technical equipment and devices that were equipped and used before the effective date of this Decree may continue to be used to detect and handle administrative violations if they still satisfy requirements prescribed in this Decree.

