Article 13. Penalties imposed upon attendants on buses, fixed-route passenger vehicles,

contract-based passenger vehicles

1. A fine ranging from VND 100.000 to VND 200.000 shall be imposed on organizations for committing one of the following violations:

a) Failing to arrange priority seats for elderly people, persons with disabilities, children, and pregnant women; failing to guide passengers to sit in designated seats;

b) Failing to wear uniforms and nametags as prescribed.
2. A fine ranging from VND 100.000 to VND 200.000 shall be imposed on attendants on buses for collecting money without giving tickets (paper or electronic) to passengers, or sells tickets at higher prices than prescribed rates.

3. A fine ranging from VND 300.000 to VND 400.000 shall be imposed on attendants on fixed- route passenger vehicles for collecting money without giving tickets (paper or electronic) to passengers, or sells tickets at higher prices than prescribed rates.
4. In addition to fines, individuals committing violations under clause 2 and clause 3 of this Article shall also be forced to return illegal profits obtained from administrative violations committed.

Article 14. Penalties for violations against regulations on internal transport operations

1. A fine ranging from VND 3.000.000 to VND 4.000.000 shall be imposed on individuals using four-wheeled motorized vehicles for internal passenger transport except for purpose of provision of passenger transport services.

2. A fine ranging from VND 3.000.000 to VND 5.000.000 shall be imposed on individuals, and from VND 6.000.000 to VND 10.000.000 shall be imposed on organizations for committing one of the following violations:
a) Failing to implement prescribed traffic safety management regulations, except for violations under point b of this clause;

b) Failing to monitor and supervise driver and vehicle operation throughout the internal transport process;
c) Operating double decker sleeper buses on mountainous roads classified as class V and VI.

d) Using internal transport vehicles for provision of passenger or goods transport services;
dd) Using internal transport vehicles to transport passengers or goods inconsistent with applicable regulations;

c) Using automobiles of cooperative members for internal transport operations without written agreements between such members and the cooperative; or using automobiles that are not under their right to enjoyment;

